  <p>Professional services ensure the job is done thoroughly without risking damage to your home or personal injury. Our team is experienced with handling severe moss and algae, ensuring your roof is restored to its best condition.</p>
</section>

<!-- FAQ accordion section -->
<section class="faq-section">
  <h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
  <div class="faq">
    <h4>Why are moss and algae common on roofs in Tampa Bay?</h4>
    <p>The Tampa Bay area has a humid, subtropical climate that provides ideal conditions for moss and algae growth. Frequent rain showers and consistent warmth create a perfect breeding ground for these organisms on shaded, moisture-retentive surfaces like roofs.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq">
    <h4>Can moss and algae damage my roof?</h4>
    <p>Yes, moss and algae can cause significant damage to roofing materials. Moss can lift and separate shingles, leading to leaks and water damage, while algae can retain moisture, encouraging rot and mold buildup. Regular maintenance is key to preventing these issues.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq">
    <h4>How can I prevent moss and algae growth on my Florida roof?</h4>
    <p>To prevent moss and algae growth, regularly inspect and clean your roof, ensure proper sunlight exposure by trimming overhanging trees, and consider installing zinc or copper strips at the peak of your roof to naturally inhibit growth.</p>
  </div>
</section>

